  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:96120",
  "description": "Ruby is an extensible, interpreted, object-oriented, scripting language. It has features to process text files and to perform system management tasks.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-93577)\n  * ruby: integer overflow issue in CI/CD regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-97229)\n  * ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-110264)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * ruby:4.0/ruby: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-9] (JIRA:RHEL-260675)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
